/-!
Useful follow-up directions include:

1. Optional chapters in this book, plus the table of contents and chapter
   dependency diagram.

2. Books and lectures on functional programming.
   For example:
   - _Learn You a Haskell for Great Good_, by Miran Lipovaca.
   - _Real World Haskell_, by Bryan O'Sullivan, John Goerzen,
     and Don Stewart.
   - ...and many other excellent books on Haskell, OCaml,
     Scheme, Racket, Scala, F sharp, etc., etc.

3. Further resources on interactive theorem proving and verification.

4. If you are interested in real-world applications of formal
   verification to critical software, see the postscript chapter of
   _Programming Language Foundations_.

5. For applications in building verified systems, the lectures and
   course materials for the 2017 DeepSpec Summer School are also a
   useful resource:
   <https://deepspec.org/event/dsss17/index.html>
-/
